    It has been said here by some that a great weapon is important to
winning nethack.  I think that great AC is worth more.  I finally won
basically because of AC after some real luck.


    I found a library on a low level with tons of scrolls.

    One blessed identify told me what they all were (I was missing only
fire, punishment and charging)

    Since I'd died many times in the past without ever using a magic marker
I decided to prepare the useless scrolls in case I found one...so I blanked
out 10 of them in fountains.  The lawful altar on level 2 allowed me to
bless them all (via holy water, of course).  I didn't realize at the time
that magic markers write on one scroll at a time.

    I found a magic lamp and the first unidentified scroll I found was
charging so I got the blessed +3 gray dragon mail (I was a Barbarian),
which I was told was the best.  Out of the three times I've wished for this
this was the first time I got +3 instead of +0.  The second wish was for an
amulet of life saving (a must in my opinion, because something bad is very
likely to happen...in my case I was eating a large corpse to gain strength
and when I thought I was answering "y" to "Do you want to stop eating" it
actually happened that the corpse was finished and the "y" meant I wanted
to eat the food in slot "y" in my pack.  Unfortunately there was a food
ration there and I choked to death).

    In any case, back to the AC, I eventually got decided to polypile some
armor and then thought...why not put the blank scrolls there too...maybe
I'll never get a marker anyway.  The scrolls became light scrolls, and on
the second polymorph became enchant armor!  To make this already long story
shorter I ended up with AC of -43 and the worst beating I took all game
after that was when the Wizard and a group of his nasties got me on the way
up.  I went from 176 hit points to 160 after many hits (then I put on the
ring of conflict).  I finished the game as a level 14 Barbarian with only
slightly more than a million points (all my gold disappeared on a throne
and I didn't often take off my ring of levitation to collect things since I
didn't want to chance drowning in hell).  I did get an unneeded amulet of
life saving from the wand of wishing and my second wish from the wand was
unusual, for "3 tins of black dragon meat" (I only got one tin...and I
didn't get the disintegration resistance that I'd hoped for).

    Summary:
	1) Great AC is important, wish for that gray dragon scale mail
	2) Get an amulet of life saving...something bad will almost
	   certainly happen (even if you can play slowly enough to avoid
	   stupid mistakes)
	3) Genocide the L's (Liches)
 
